-- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/14-4-live-integration-test-runs-c70-close.md:19,58,203,238` and `_bmad-output/cross-llm-reviews/story-14-4-review-prompt.md:32,44,59,301,340,485,520` still cite Epic 12 retro Action #4 as `L162`, but `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/epic-12-retro-2026-06-01.md:163` is the actual Action #4 line. That breaks the Story 14.3 Codex HIGH-A “all citations verified pre-write” claim and leaves the review prompt auditing the wrong source line. Concrete fix: change every `Epic 12 ... L162 Action #4` reference in the story spec and review prompt to `L163`.
-
-- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:246-277` installs only Python dependencies and then immediately probes `codex`, `copilot`, and `claude`, but `pyproject.toml:79-90` documents that the Codex/Copilot CLIs must already be on `$PATH`, and the live tests explicitly skip when those binaries are absent (`tests/integration/test_codex_cli_live.py:40-42`, `tests/integration/test_copilot_cli_live.py:25-27`). As written, the new `ubuntu-latest` job has no repo-owned mechanism to make the CLI half of the story actually run, so `_TESTED_UP_TO` verification for Codex/Copilot/Claude is best-effort rather than delivered behavior. Concrete fix: either add explicit CLI installation steps in the workflow, or move this job to a runner image/self-hosted label that guarantees those binaries and document that prerequisite in the job comment/spec.
-
-MED
-
-- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:268-273` does not implement the advertised `NOT FOUND` fallback correctly. `observed="$($bin --version 2>&1 | head -1 || echo 'NOT FOUND')"` runs inside a pipeline without `pipefail`, so a missing binary yields the shell error text instead of `NOT FOUND` (reproduced locally with `missingbinary --version 2>&1 | head -1`). Concrete fix: replace the pipeline with an explicit `command -v "$bin" >/dev/null 2>&1` guard, or enable `set -o pipefail` and branch before invoking `head`.
-
-- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:215-219` tells the operator the wrong secrets-to-tests mapping. It says `OPENAI_API_KEY` is used by `judge`/`judge_calibrate` and `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` only by `claude_agent_sdk`, but the judge live tests actually gate on `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (`tests/integration/test_judge_live.py:34-35`, `tests/integration/test_judge_calibrate_live.py:42-43`), while `OPENAI_API_KEY` is for `openai_agents_sdk` and Codex (`tests/integration/test_openai_agents_sdk_live.py:42-44`, plus the codex note). An operator who follows the current comment can configure the wrong secret set and get fake “expected” skips. Concrete fix: rewrite the prerequisite block so `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is called out for `claude_agent_sdk`, `judge`, and `judge_calibrate`, and `OPENAI_API_KEY` is called out for `openai_agents_sdk` and Codex.
-
-- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:321-327` reports an all-skipped run as “all live test files exited cleanly” with no explicit “nothing actually executed” notice. Because these tests are env/binary gated, the common failure mode here is six skips or zero passes, and this summary reads much closer to success than to “operator prerequisites missing,” which weakens the mechanism-vs-evidence framing the story is trying to preserve. Concrete fix: track aggregate passed/skipped totals and emit a separate summary/`::notice::` when `passed == 0` (or all files are skipped / exit 5) telling the operator that no live evidence was produced and secrets/binaries still need to be configured.
-
-- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml:38` still says `last_updated: 2026-06-03`, but the Story 14.4 spec claims the file was advanced to `2026-06-04` (`_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/14-4-live-integration-test-runs-c70-close.md:139,226`). This leaves the project status ledger internally inconsistent on the story’s own acceptance criteria. Concrete fix: bump `last_updated` in `sprint-status.yaml` to `2026-06-04` when landing Story 14.4, or remove the claim from the story if that field is intentionally not touched.
-
-LOW
-
-- `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/14-4-live-integration-test-runs-c70-close.md:155,246,258` and `_bmad-output/cross-llm-reviews/story-14-4-review-prompt.md:15,93,437,528,540` hardcode the workflow change as `+60 lines` / `269 → 329`, but `git show HEAD:.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml | wc -l` is `210` and the current diff is `@@ -208,3 +208,122` / `119 insertions` by `git diff --stat`. The review prompt even asks reviewers to validate a delta that the current tree cannot satisfy. Concrete fix: update the line-count claims to match HEAD, or stop pinning an exact delta and describe the job structurally instead.

