    12	
    13	- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:321-327` reports an all-skipped / zero-pass run as “all live test files exited cleanly” with no explicit notice that no live evidence was actually produced. That weakens the story’s mechanism-vs-evidence framing in the exact operator-misconfiguration path the workflow is supposed to make honest. Concrete fix: track aggregate `passed`/`skipped` totals and emit a separate summary line plus `::notice::` when `passed == 0` (or all files are skipped / exit 5) telling the operator to configure the missing prerequisites before treating the run as evidence.
