-- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:268-273` does not implement the advertised `NOT FOUND` fallback correctly. `observed="$($bin --version 2>&1 | head -1 || echo 'NOT FOUND')"` runs inside a pipeline without `pipefail`, so a missing binary yields the shell error text instead of `NOT FOUND` (reproduced locally with `missingbinary --version 2>&1 | head -1`). Concrete fix: replace the pipeline with an explicit `command -v "$bin" >/dev/null 2>&1` guard, or enable `set -o pipefail` and branch before invoking `head`.
+- `.github/workflows/dogfood-integration.yml:268-273` does not implement the advertised `NOT FOUND` fallback correctly. `observed="$($bin --version 2>&1 | head -1 || echo 'NOT FOUND')"` runs in a pipeline without `pipefail`, so a missing binary yields the shell error text instead of `NOT FOUND` (reproduced locally with a fake binary name). Concrete fix: guard with `command -v "$bin" >/dev/null 2>&1` before invocation, or branch on the command result instead of relying on `||` after `head`.
